WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.281
Your bench is ESD-safe.

00:00:04.561 --> 00:00:07.183
But what about the floor your team walks across to reach it?

00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:13.015
Static builds as people walk, and parts travel between benches, racks and trolleys.

00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:17.141
A safe bench alone cannot protect a board while it is being carried.

00:00:17.741 --> 00:00:25.423
Full ESD control works in layers: ESD worktops or mats on benches, wrist straps on operators,

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:31.287
ESD footwear, and ESD flooring that carries charge away as people move.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.086
Each layer covers a gap that the others miss.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:38.843
Trolleys and racks that carry boards between areas need thinking about too.

00:00:39.443 --> 00:00:45.869
Furnisys provides the bench layer: ESD workstations, mats, wrist straps and grounding kits.

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:50.265
Flooring is outside our range, but on one oil and gas PCB lab,

00:00:50.265 --> 00:00:56.041
we connected the client with a flooring provider so protection ran from bench to floor.

00:00:56.641 --> 00:00:58.816
So map every place your boards travel.

00:00:59.096 --> 00:01:00.134
Where are your gaps?

00:01:00.414 --> 00:01:04.884
Comment below, and next, start our modular series with the Link Uprighter.

00:01:05.484 --> 00:01:09.729
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

